{"module":"Term 2","title":"Unit 10 — Economy","description":"Work, money and trade; gerund and infinitive; expressing purpose.","intro":"This unit deals with jobs, money, trade and economic development.","objectifs":["Use vocabulary of jobs and money.","Choose between gerund and infinitive.","Express purpose with to / in order to / so that."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary","h":"<ul><li>a salary, unemployment, to earn, to save, to borrow, to lend, a loan, a budget, export / import, a company, a customer, a small business</li><li>jobs: engineer, accountant, farmer, nurse, entrepreneur</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: gerund or infinitive","h":"<table><tr><th>+ verb-ing</th><th>+ to + verb</th></tr><tr><td>enjoy, avoid, finish, mind, keep, practise</td><td>want, decide, hope, plan, need, afford, learn</td></tr><tr><td>after prepositions: interested in saving</td><td>after adjectives: easy to understand</td></tr></table>"},{"t":"Expressing purpose","h":"<ul><li><b>to / in order to / so as to</b> + base verb: <i>She works hard <b>to</b> save money.</i></li><li><b>so that</b> + clause: <i>He opened a shop <b>so that</b> he could support his family.</i></li></ul><div class=\"box note\"><span class=\"box-title\">borrow / lend</span><p>You <b>borrow</b> money <b>from</b> someone; someone <b>lends</b> money <b>to</b> you.</p></div>"}],"recap":"enjoy / avoid / finish + -ing ; want / decide / hope + to + verb ; preposition + -ing. Purpose: to / in order to + verb ; so that + clause. borrow from / lend to.","cards":[["avoid","+ verb-ing"],["decide","+ to + verb"],["in order to","+ base verb (purpose)"],["borrow / lend","borrow from ; lend to"]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"I want ___ an engineer.","choices":["to become","becoming","become","became"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Want” + to + verb."},{"type":"direct","q":"Money you receive for your work every month is a ___.","accept":["salary"],"display":"salary","explain":"A monthly payment for a job = a salary."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Selling products to other countries is…","choices":["export","import","a loan","unemployment"],"answer":0,"explain":"Export = send goods abroad to sell."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"She avoids ___ money on useless things.","choices":["spending","to spend","spend","spent"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Avoid” + verb-ing."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “He works at night ___ order to pay for his studies.”","accept":["in"],"display":"in","explain":"“In order to” + base verb = purpose."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Can you ___ me 50 dirhams? I’ll give it back tomorrow.","choices":["lend","borrow","earn","save"],"answer":0,"explain":"Someone gives you money temporarily → lend (to me)."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Find the correct sentence:","choices":["I’m interested in starting a small business.","I’m interested to start a small business.","I’m interested in start a small business.","I’m interesting in starting a small business."],"answer":0,"explain":"After a preposition (in) → verb-ing."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: “They saved money so ___ they could buy a house.”","accept":["that"],"display":"that","explain":"“So that” + clause expresses purpose."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“My parents decided ___ a new car.”","choices":["to buy","buying","buy","bought"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Decide” + to + verb."}]}}